n lower than pre-war levels, Bloomberg has reported, citing energy consultancies.\n\nOil purchases by Chinese refiners are climbing back towards 10 million barrels daily but may not hit that number until the end of the year, according to analysts from Rystad Energy, Energy Aspects, and FGE NexantECA. Fourth-q", "citation": "China\u2019s Oil Imports Set to Rebound as Refiners Hunt for New Supply \u2014 OilPrice, 2026-08-21. https://oilprice.com/Latest-Energy-News/World-News/Chinas-Oil-Imports-Set-to-Rebound-as-Refiners-Hunt-for-New-Supply.html"}, {"title": "India bonds hang tight before supply as oil stalls", "feed": "ET Markets", "ts": "2026-08-21T07:58:11+00:00", "url": "https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/bonds/india-bonds-hang-tight-before-supply-as-oil-stalls/articleshow/133397733.cms", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "On Friday morning, Indian government bonds found stability as oil prices leveled off. The market reacted to hawkish minutes from the central bank and a sudden spike in crude prices. Later today, a major debt sale will gauge investor interest in bonds. As retail inflation surpassed the Reserve Bank of India's target, rising oil prices and global yields will influence the upcoming market direction.\n\nHDFC Bank has achieved a remarkable feat by securing $1.75 billion through a dual-tranche dollar bond issuance, marking the largest single debt fundraising effort by any Indian bank. This successful venture included selling five-year bonds worth $1.25 billion and three-year bonds worth $500 million", "citation": "India bonds hang tight before supply as oil stalls \u2014 ET Markets, 2026-08-21. https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/markets/bonds/india-bonds-hang-tight-before-supply-as-oil-stalls/articleshow/133397733.cms"}, {"title": "Nifty flatlines near 24,232 at midday; crude surge caps gains, Power Grid shines", "feed": "BusinessLine Mkts", "ts": "2026-08-21T07:52:31+00:00", "url": "https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/nifty-flatlines-near-24232-at-midday-crude-surge-caps-gains-power-grid-shines/article71372689.ece", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "Bank Nifty displayed relative strength, with HDFC Bank, Kotak Mahindra Bank, and ICICI Bank identified as the top three contributors to Nifty\u2019s gains at midday.\n\nMarkets were trading nearly flat at midday on Friday, with benchmark indices struggling to hold on to early gains as a sharp surge in crude oil prices and renewed rise in US Treasury yields dampened risk appetite. At 12.51 pm, the Sensex was at 77,549.90, up just 12.18 points or 0.02 per cent, while the Nifty 50 was at 24,232.55, up a marginal 0.70 points or 0.00 per cent, against a previous close of 24,231.85. The Nifty remained confined to a tight trading band through the session, with limited directional momentum.\n\nSudeep Shah, H", "citation": "Nifty flatlines near 24,232 at midday; crude surge caps gains, Power Grid shines \u2014 BusinessLine Mkts, 2026-08-21. https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/nifty-flatlines-near-24232-at-midday-crude-surge-caps-gains-power-grid-shines/article71372689.ece"}], "primary_sources": [{"series": "wti", "name": "Yahoo \u00b7 CL=F", "url": "https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/CL=F"}, {"series": "wti", "name": "EIA Weekly Petroleum Status", "url": "https://www.eia.gov/petroleum/supply/weekly/"}], "analogues": {"member_z_today": {"wti": -0.94}, "analogues": [{"date": "2026-05-22", "distance": 0.0, "member_z": {"wti": -0.94}}, {"date": "2025-10-22", "distance": 0.01, "member_z": {"wti": -0.93}}, {"date": "2025-04-29", "distance": 0.01, "member_z": {"wti": -0.92}}, {"date": "2024-10-31", "distance": 0.02, "member_z": {"wti": -0.95}}, {"date": "2025-08-20", "distance": 0.02, "member_z": {"wti": -0.91}}], "aftermath": {"wti": {"stats": {"+5d": {"n": 5, "median_pct": 1.49, "hit_rate_up": 0.6, "min_pct": -9.57, "max_pct": 4.48}, "+20d": {"n": 3, "median_pct": 1.33, "hit_rate_up": 1.0, "min_pct": 0.78, "max_pct": 3.83}}, "median_path": [0.0, 0.33, 0.71, 2.52, 0.0